  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_037: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, ViT-L, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.706 accuracy. In the RNA-only regime, transformer aggregation gave only a negligible 0.3-point gain over avgpool (config_006 vs config_005), suggesting aggregation is not a major bottleneck. However, that comparison was made without an image modality; in the multimodal setting, the aggregation step operates on RNA profiles before fusion with image features, and a more expressive aggregation could theoretically capture profile-level structure that better complements the image signal. Config_039 is a clean single-variable change from the current best (avgpool → transformer), isolating the aggregation effect in the multimodal ViT-L + weighted fusion context. If it yields a meaningful gain, it identifies a new best and a productive direction; if it confirms the RNA-only finding of negligible difference, it definitively rules out aggregation as a remaining lever, allowing us to redirect remaining budget toward other design axes (e.g., fusion refinement or encoder scaling) with confidence. Under the limited budget, this is the highest-information single-variable test available from the current frontier."
}

